    <string name="settings_about">About</string>
    <string name="settings_about_body">VirtualCam Manager v%1$s\nPure Magisk + Zygisk (no LSPosed).\nNative OpenGL interception + AMediaCodec.\nDevice verification is required before claiming a full camera spoof.</string>

    <!-- 架构页 -->
    <string name="arch_title">Architecture</string>
    <string name="arch_headline">Pure Magisk + Single APK</string>
    <string name="arch_works_title">What works now (v%1$s)</string>
    <string name="arch_works_body">• Magisk module + Zygisk native library (multi-ABI, 16 KB pages)\n• This APK manages virtual.mp4 and the enable flag (3-step flow)\n• No LSPosed / Xposed / second framework\n• Native OpenGL interception (ShadowHook on glBindTexture / glDraw*)\n• AMediaCodec continuous decode → RGB texture upload\n• Status written to /data/adb/virtualcam/hook_status</string>
    <string name="arch_limit_title">Honest limitation</string>
    <string name="arch_limit_body">The current GL path uploads RGB into a GL_TEXTURE_2D and redirects EXTERNAL_OES binds. Many Camera2 / CameraX shaders use samplerExternalOES and may ignore a 2D texture. An OES SurfaceTexture / EGLImage path is the next step for broader app coverage.\n\nDo not treat this as a full camera spoof until real apps show the virtual feed on device.</string>
    <string name="arch_install_title">Install (3 steps)</string>
    <string name="arch_install_body">1. Magisk → Zygisk ON → flash the module zip → reboot\n2. Install this Manager APK → grant root\n3. Home → pick a video or image → turn VirtualCam ON → open any camera app</string>
    <string name="arch_files_title">Control plane files</string>
    <string name="arch_files_body">/data/adb/virtualcam/enabled\n/data/adb/virtualcam/hook_status\n/data/adb/virtualcam/virtual.mp4  (fallback)\n/storage/emulated/0/DCIM/Camera1/virtual.mp4  (primary)</string>

